

(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[1 1 "//go:build linux"] [19 1 "// The module _socket (PY6e; Modules/socketmodule.c): BSD sockets over Go's syscall, for socket.py and what imports"] [20 1 "// it (doctest through pdb, subprocess's and asyncio's loopback pairs, test.support.socket_helper). A socket object"] [21 1 "// keeps its descriptor, family, type, protocol and timeout; a timeout is CPython's: the descriptor non-blocking and"] [22 1 "// each operation waiting on select(2) for at most the timeout (sock_call_ex). Addresses are CPython's tuples for"] [23 1 "// AF_INET and AF_INET6, a str or bytes path for AF_UNIX (a leading NUL: Linux's abstract namespace). Names resolve"] [24 1 "// as musl's getaddrinfo does through /etc/hosts and /etc/services (no DNS query: the tests run on loopback only)."] [31 29 "// seconds; < 0: blocking, no timeout"] [44 1 "// sockErr is a Go error of a socket call as OSError's subclass of its errno."] [47 14 "// a signal handler's exception from an interrupted wait (queue 231)"] [55 1 "// errnoError is OSError(errno, strerror(errno)[, filename]): its subclass by errno."] [90 1 "// wait is select(2) on the socket for reading or writing, at most its timeout; false when it timed out."] [98 4 "// queue 231: the wait in ppoll with the wake pipe, a signal's handler run as at EINTR (sock_call's loop)"] [117 25 "// the GIL released while it blocks (PY6f's allowThreads; queue 200, PY6-core)"] [134 1 "// call runs op as CPython's sock_call: with a timeout, after waiting until the socket is ready, again while it"] [135 1 "// would block; without one, once (a blocking socket, or a non-blocking one's BlockingIOError)."] [143 40 "// the GIL released while it blocks (PY6f's allowThreads; queue 200, PY6-core)"] [184 1 "// timeoutArg is a timeout argument: None (-1) or a non-negative number of seconds."] [209 1 "// ---- addresses"] [217 5 "// IDNA: the names the tests use are ASCII; a non-ASCII one is encoded as CPython's idna codec does"] [237 1 "// resolveOne is a host's address of family (setipaddr): ” any, '<broadcast>', a literal, else /etc/hosts' first."] [296 1 "// precedence is RFC 3484's policy table, as musl sorts getaddrinfo's results (::1 first)."] [307 1 "// resolveHost is musl's name lookup: a numeric host, else the lines of /etc/hosts naming it, each address once,"] [308 1 "// sorted by precedence; canon the first line's canonical name (the literal for a numeric host)."] [312 24 "// AI_V4MAPPED"] [327 4 "// inet_aton's forms: 127.1, 0x7f.1, a single number"] [333 22 "// AI_NUMERICHOST"] [366 1 "// inetAton is inet_aton(3): a.b.c.d, a.b.c, a.b or a, each part decimal, octal or hex."] [418 1 "// sockaddrArg is getsockaddrarg: an address object of the socket's family as a syscall.Sockaddr."] [450 23 "// a file named \"@...\": Go's SockaddrUnix reads a leading '@' as the abstract namespace"] [530 1 "// unixSockName is getsockname or getpeername (call) of an AF_UNIX socket as makesockaddr makes it from the address and"] [531 1 "// its length (py-os-1124): Go's anyToSockaddr ends a path at its first NUL, so a Linux abstract name holding NULs"] [532 1 "// (test_socket's TestLinuxAbstractNamespace) came back cut; here an abstract name (a NUL first) is the bytes of the"] [533 1 "// whole length, a path the bytes up to its NUL decoded as a file name, none \"\"."] [560 1 "// sockaddrObj is makesockaddr: a syscall.Sockaddr as CPython's address object."] [569 22 "// unnamed (Go's anyToSockaddr turns its empty path's NUL into '@')"] [588 1 "// ---- buffers"] [590 1 "// writableBuf is a writable bytes-like object's bytes: a bytearray, or a memoryview of one."] [596 19 "// queue 231: an array's buffer is writable (recvmsg_into's testRecvmsgIntoArray)"] [612 2 "// a class's __buffer__ (queue 231: sendmsg's reentrant buffer), its view taken as Py_buffer is"] [654 3 "// sock_initobj_impl's audit (queue 536): the arguments as given (-1 for one not given)"] [800 61 "// sock_bind's audit (queue 536)"] [838 5 "// Go's Accept4 refuses the family it has no Sockaddr of; C's accept of AF_ALG has no address"] [862 25 "// the GIL released while it blocks (PY6f's allowThreads; queue 200, PY6-core)"] [1172 3 "// sock_sendmsg_iovec: the parts taken as a tuple first (PySequence_Tuple), so a part's __buffer__ that changes"] [1173 3 "// the sequence changes nothing sent (queue 249: test_sendmsg_reentrant_data_mutation)"] [1191 35 "// PySequence_Tuple, as the data's"] [1199 5 "// any sequence of length 3, as PySequence_Fast takes it (queue 231: test_aead_aes_gcm's lists)"] [1486 55 "// queue 536"] [1663 4 "// an int port outside 0-65535 as its decimal text, as CPython passes every int (PyObject_Str), the C"] [1664 4 "// library's to judge (gh-74895: no OverflowError; musl's EAI_SERVICE; queue 284)"] [1724 21 "// NI_NUMERICHOST"] [1727 29 "// NI_NAMEREQD"] [1732 21 "// NI_NUMERICSERV"] [1734 23 "// NI_DGRAM"] [1917 4 "// CPython's get_CMSG_LEN and get_CMSG_SPACE: the length at most socklen_t's limit less CMSG_LEN(0),"] [1918 4 "// or less CMSG_SPACE(1)"] [1934 1 "// hostsName is /etc/hosts' canonical name of an address, \"\" when none."] [2002 1 "// getaddrinfo is musl's: the host's addresses (numeric, /etc/hosts; None: loopback, or any with AI_PASSIVE) times"] [2003 1 "// the socket types asked (0: stream and datagram), canonname always set as musl sets it."] [2010 19 "// musl's __lookup_serv: a numeric service past 65535 is EAI_SERVICE"] [2014 32 "// AI_NUMERICSERV"] [2039 21 "// AI_PASSIVE"]] :go/pos {:name [3 9] :package [3 1]} :go/semis [[46 27] [49 34] [104 40] [177 46] [280 39] [310 36] [322 36] [326 29] [328 30] [388 12] [388 21] [398 12] [398 21] [433 53] [511 36] [519 44] [521 42] [537 77] [551 44] [554 55] [601 29] [609 24] [613 34] [617 26] [625 24] [655 104] [756 31] [767 48] [778 49] [797 42] [800 46] [810 36] [827 43] [883 36] [891 45] [907 48] [926 42] [949 45] [985 36] [1026 42] [1045 46] [1089 33] [1118 45] [1127 37] [1146 50] [1152 37] [1169 45] [1230 6] [1240 51] [1260 46] 